{
  "name": "history-oct-to-apr-18-month-transition-start",
  "description": "A fixed-date calendar that changes from 1 October to 1 April years through an eighteen-month transition year, 2024-10-01 to 2026-03-31, split into six quarters of three calendar months. The dates and the six quarters are those of research/filers/siemens-india.md; the quarter split and the week block are illustrative. Numbered by 'start', the years around the change are 2023, 2024 (the transition), 2026: 2025 is skipped at the change. shift of a year moves along the sequence of fiscal years, not by the number. A skipped number lies inside the supported range: period with year 2025 is PERIOD_NOT_FOUND at year, a period argument naming it is PERIOD_NOT_FOUND at period, years(2025, 2025) is empty, and a label that names it is LABEL_NOT_RECOGNISED. Scheme 'short' writes 'FY24-26' with {yy}, century_pivot 2069 and {yy_end}.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "oracle",
    "citation": "Independent implementation of the spec in conformance/generators/fiscal_oracle.py, written with Python datetime and no fiscalclock code",
    "url": null,
    "checked_by": "fiscal_oracle.py: Calendar.seq built from the regimes and transitions; change_errors and naming_errors pass"
  },
